>>
>> Old freyburgerd-Doug.NetHack-saved-game
>> New doug.freyburger-Doug.NetHack-saved-game
>>
>> Moving to a new OS probably won't work.  Moving version of Windows to
>> version of Windows, I don't know if it will work.
> Okay, thanks. I didn't know that different OSes used different save
> formats, but that wasn't my problem! I was just asking how to play
> from two different Win32 computers.
In that case, your best bet is to copy the whole NetHack directory 
(including the binaries) to the new system.  This should keep your high 
score list as well as the saved games intact (possibly after renaming 
the latter) and it make sure as well that you don't have problems with 
different patches in different binaries.


